# admin/.env.example — documentation only.
#
# The admin portal is static vanilla HTML; browsers cannot read .env files.
# Nothing here is a runtime dependency for local development:
#
#   1. The Supabase publishable key is already embedded in
#      src/supabaseClient.js (it is public and safe to hardcode). No secret
#      key is ever used in the browser.
#   2. The Supabase service-role key is ONLY used by the Ap-ro backend
#      (Ap-ro/.env). Never put it here.
#
# Deploying the admin portal on its own origin (e.g. b.com):
#   Set the Backend Services API origin on every admin page BEFORE admin.js:
#       <script>window.APERO_API_BASE = "https://aperonight.fun";</script>
#   This is consumed by admin.js's apiFetch() for:
#       POST /api/admin/refunds   (process a refund via PaymentService)
#       GET  /api/admin/export    (CSV download)
#
# Local development:
#   Run `npm run dev` in Ap-ro — server.js also mounts this admin folder at
#   http://localhost:5000/admin, so /api works on the same origin and no
#   APERO_API_BASE override is needed.
#
# Example values for reference (never commit real ones):
#   SUPABASE_URL=      https://ijgfebtxleogmmeejkpe.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY= sb_publishable_...
#   APERO_API_BASE=    https://aperonight.fun